# Vulnerability: Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)

## The Problem

If `req.query.q` is reflected directly into HTML without encoding, an attacker can inject malicious JavaScript:

```javascript
// Vulnerable code
app.get('/search', (req, res) => {
  res.send(`<h1>Search results for: ${req.query.q}</h1>`);
});
```

**Attack:**
```
/search?q=<script>alert('XSS')</script>
